WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.868
The evaluation uses a range of compute graphs.

00:00:02.948 --> 00:00:07.419
The main scaling study is on four random layered
graphs, G1 through G4,

00:00:07.499 --> 00:00:12.867
whose sizes grow from one hundred nodes and a
couple hundred edges up to one thousand

00:00:12.947 --> 00:00:15.174
nodes and nearly six thousand edges.

00:00:15.254 --> 00:00:20.942
There is also a real-world compute graph with four
hundred forty-two nodes and over twelve

00:00:21.022 --> 00:00:23.955
hundred edges used for the headline comparison.

00:00:24.035 --> 00:00:29.595
For every graph the memory budget is set to eighty
and ninety percent of the peak memory

00:00:29.675 --> 00:00:32.799
of the initial schedule without rematerialization,

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:36.260
so the solver is forced to actually recompute tensors.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:41.580
All experiments run on a sixteen-core workstation
with thirty-two gigabytes of RAM.
